+    - id: gotcha-evidence-boundary
       priority: high
-      text: Compiler, schema, link, and portability success prove package invariants, not that the skill makes correct decisions on realistic tasks.
-    - id: gotcha-no-leaked-forward-test
+      text: A green structural check cannot prove a behavioral claim; use the methodology's claim-specific evidence boundary.
+    - id: gotcha-trial-exposure
       priority: high
-      text: Do not call a forward-test blind when the evaluator received the suspected defect, expected answer, intended fix, or prior conclusions.
-    - id: gotcha-rendered-surface
+      text: A trial executor exposed to a diagnosis or answer key is not blind; distinguish it from the assessor who needs the rubric.
+    - id: gotcha-shipped-readback
       priority: medium
-      text: Inspect rendered or packaged readback when syntax, links, generated output, or markup can disappear despite structural validation.
+      text: A correct source does not erase defective installed instructions; inspect the surface the executor receives.
   policies:
-    - id: policy-capability-first
-      title: Capability-first review
-      text: Judge the skill by the decisions, actions, artifacts, and handoffs it reliably produces for its declared actor or consumer, not by package completeness or instruction volume.
-    - id: policy-reviewer-action-boundary
-      title: Reviewer action boundary
-      text: Read and inspect in-scope local artifacts by default. Do not mutate the reviewed snapshot; use a disposable copy for checks that may write, and require separate authority for external, destructive, costly, or scope-expanding actions.
-    - id: policy-grounded-findings
-      title: Grounded findings
-      text: Attach each material claim to inspected evidence, label reviewer inference and source conflict, and report missing evidence without turning absence in the reviewed scope into a factual no.
-    - id: policy-output-contract
-      title: Review output contract
-      text: Start with one plain-language outcome sentence, then report mode, assurance, snapshot, scope, capability and anti-claims, surface inventory, reviewer actions, findings with evidence basis and impact, structural and rendered/package readback, runtime/test and forward-test results, remediation status when applicable, verdict, and next owner.
-    - id: policy-bounded-remediation-reaudit
-      title: Bounded remediation re-audit
-      text: Re-audit accepted prior findings on a new stable snapshot using the remediation delta, original failure paths, closure evidence, and blast-radius surface. Skip unchanged verified package scope and reject cosmetic-only closure; widen when capability, authority, trigger, output, runtime behavior, or material scope changed or blast radius is unbounded.
+    - id: policy-methodology-owner
+      title: Review contract owner
+      text: Methodology owns review modes, assurance, action limits, severity, verdict ordering, re-audit scope, and output. Apply those rules to the requested boundary rather than expanding every review into a full audit.
+    - id: policy-behavioral-evidence-owner
+      title: Behavioral evidence owner
+      text: Forward-testing owns case preparation, exposure, execution and assessment. It supplies bounded evidence, not an independent verdict by itself.
   portability:
     required: true
     rules:
-      - Do not require repository-specific paths, session stores, or external local files to perform a review.
-      - Keep all mandatory review and verdict rules inside this skill folder.
-      - Treat repository commands and source precedence as discovered target context, not universal contracts.
-      - Keep runtime-specific discovery in the invoking agent's instructions unless the target skill explicitly owns that runtime.
+      - Keep mandatory review and verdict guidance inside this folder; discover repository rules and commands from the target context.
+      - Declare tools, external facts, and specialized expertise needed for particular claims; unavailable dependencies limit those claims, not the entire local method.
+      - Keep runtime-specific session or log discovery with the invoking agent unless the target explicitly owns that runtime.
     checklist:
-      - Confirm the package works when copied without repository history or the sessions that informed its design.
-      - Confirm every mandatory reference is reachable from SKILL.md.
-      - Confirm UI metadata matches the trigger and does not imply remediation ownership.
-      - Confirm no runtime, scripts, tests, metrics, or commands are claimed for this documentation-only skill.
+      - Confirm required references are reachable and the local method is usable without repository history.
+      - Confirm metadata represents review scope and assurance without implying remediation authority.
+      - Do not claim a runtime, scripts, tests, metrics, or CLI for this documentation-only skill.
